const faq = [
  {
    q: 'What does buying an apartment in Spain cost on top of the price?',
    a: 'For a resale apartment in Andalucía you pay 7% transfer tax (ITP), plus around 1 to 2% for the notary, land registry, lawyer and possibly a gestor. For a new build from a developer you pay 10% VAT and 1.2% stamp duty (AJD). In total, allow 10 to 13% on top of the price.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is a derrama?',
    a: 'A one-off levy that the community of owners charges for a large expense, such as a new roof, a lift or repairing the facade. If it was agreed before the sale, settle in the contract who pays it. Otherwise it often falls to the new owner.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I let my apartment to tourists?',
    a: 'Only with a registration with the Junta de Andalucía and a national registration number. Since April 2025, new holiday lets in an apartment building also need the approval of three fifths of the owners, unless the statutes already allow it. Some buildings ban it altogether.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do the parking space and storeroom come with the apartment?',
    a: 'Not always. A parking space (plaza de garaje) or storeroom (trastero) is often a separate property in the land registry. Check the nota simple to see whether they are included and whether they are transferred separately.',
  },
];
